A||||2||deceler8||Getting B&W VGA monitor working w/Win95||||1||
Z||000000||deceler8||06-19-2001||02:20 PM||||A friend of mine picked up a surplus computer from her company (without monitor) for $25...it's a Gateway Pentium with Windows 95 installed. I gave her an old Philips VGA B&W monitor and it works initially (displays the Windows 95 logo and such) but gets all fuzzy when Windows actually starts.<P>It also works with Windows in safe mode, but how do I change the video settings so this monitor will work ?<P>If I start Windows normally, the monitor gets wierd and I can't get into Control Panel<P>Anyone ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||84Bill||06-19-2001||02:30 PM||||Yep start it in safe mode then change the monitor to a 640x480 standard monitor.<P>The problem is that the monitor either cant handel the higher resolutions like 1024x768 or the higher refresh rates usually above 70hz refresh is higher 65 is standard low||||reg||14
Z||000002||fierospeeder||06-19-2001||05:22 PM||||do what 84bill said, find the driver for the lowest grade monitor.<P>I use to have an old monitor and it was really bad.  Windows 98 now has a message window that pops up when you change your settings.  Some of the old monitors cant handle the resolution and will go totaly blank with fuzz.  What you do is wait a few seconds without touching anything, mouse, or keyboard, and windows will restore your original settings.  Otherwise you have to restart in safemode.<P>also change to 16 colors, and the lowest resolution in your display properties||||reg||1
